use estimate-template.flow
use estimate-rules.flow
use estimate-draft-rules.flow
use ../knowledge/tool-knowledge.flow

do Require explicit Jira publication in @request. Resolve and retain the local
    project and ticket identity, and read the selected estimate under @draft_rules.
    Return an object with project, ticket_id (null if unknown), path, and text. as @state

if @state.ticket_id == null
    ask "Which Jira ticket should this estimate use?" as @ticket_input
    do Validate @ticket_input as one Jira ID against the current task and draft
        association. Bind an unassigned draft, retain task identity, and return
        @state updated with that ID. as @state

do Require a complete @state.text matching @estimate_template and @estimate_rules.
    Stop on missing or invalid content; do not rewrite.

do Resolve private absolute acli and adf using @tool_guidance.
    Return an object with acli and adf. as @tools

run @tools.acli jira workitem comment list --key @state.ticket_id --json --paginate as @comments_result

do Parse @comments_result.stdout as JSON. Check material clarifications and
    identical estimate comments against @state.text. Return an object with
    Boolean evidence_contradicts_draft and identical_comment, and duplicate_url.
    Never replace unrelated comments. as @comment_state

if @comment_state.evidence_contradicts_draft == true
    return "Publication stopped: Jira evidence contradicts the draft. Run /inux estimate improve with the new evidence; the draft is unchanged."

if @comment_state.identical_comment == false
    do Publish @state.text as one bounded transaction following @tool_guidance.
        Create a unique private temporary directory and .adf output path. Run @tools.adf
        with separate arguments @state.path and the output path; verify faithful
        conversion. Immediately recheck active project, ticket, and saved text
        against @state; stop on any change. Run @tools.acli with separate arguments
        jira, workitem, comment, create, --key, @state.ticket_id, --body-file,
        the ADF path, and --json. Parse and verify the comment URL, looking it up
        only if absent. Clean only this transaction's temporary directory on
        success or failure. Return the verified URL. as @publication_url
else
    set publication_url = @comment_state.duplicate_url

do Verify @publication_url identifies the published or identical existing
    comment for @state.ticket_id. Keep the Markdown on an uncertain result.

do Apply verified-publication cleanup to @state.path under @draft_rules,
    preserving the file if it no longer matches @state.text. Return the cleanup
    result, including any retained path. as @cleanup_result

print Report @state.ticket_id, @publication_url, and @cleanup_result briefly.
